CSE103 — LAB 3

Question 3.3: Push Projects to GitHub

Name: Sourav
Email: souravjaat815@gmail.com

GitHub Repository:
https://github.com/sourav8282/cse103-lab-LAB3

Step 1: Link Local Repository to GitHub

Commands:
git remote -v

Step 2: Push Commits to GitHub

Commands:
git add .
git commit -m "Add main.py and README"
git push -u origin main

Step 3: Push Another Commit

Commands:
git add CHANGELOG.md
git commit -m "docs: add changelog file"
git push

Step 4: Pull Changes From GitHub

Commands:
git pull
cat README.md

Step 5: View Updated Commit History

Command:
git log --oneline

Conclusion:
Successfully connected the local Git repository to GitHub, pushed commits, created a changelog file, and pulled remote updates.
